t in modern times there is no such restriction."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dengke-mas-naniura"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dengke_mas_naniura"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":10,"links":[["Andaliman","ingredient/andaliman"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Chili powder","ingredient/chili-powder"],["Common carp","ingredient/common-carp"],["Etlingera elatior","ingredient/etlingera-elatior"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Lime","ingredient/lime"],["Red onion","ingredient/red-onion"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"],["Gepuk","dish/gepuk"]]}]},"ingredient/honeycomb":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/honeycomb","n":"Honeycomb","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["A honeycomb is a mass of hexagonal prismatic cells built from beeswax by honey bees in their nests to contain their brood (eggs, larvae, and pupae) and stores of honey and pollen."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-honeycomb"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honeycomb"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Cambodian cuisine","cuisine/cambodian-cuisine",[["Grilled honeycomb","dish/grilled-honeycomb"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Spring onions","ingredient/spring-onions"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/f7/Honey_comb.jpg/500px-Honey_comb.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Merdal at Turkish Wikipedia","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Honey_comb.jpg"}},"dish/seattle-style-hot-dog":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/seattle-style-hot-dog","n":"Seattle-style hot dog","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A Seattle-style hot dog, locally referred to as a Seattle Dog, is a hot dog served in a bun slathered with cream cheese and topped with caramelized onions and sometimes jalapeños. In Seattle, the dogs are sold from food carts, especially outside stadiums on game day and as a late-night meal outside the city's music venues."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-seattle-style-hot-dog"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seattle-style_hot_dog"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Western American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states"],["Pacific Northwest cuisine","cuisine/pacific-northwest-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Bialy","ingredient/bialy"],["Bialy (bread)","ingredient/bialy-bread"],["Cream cheese","ingredient/cream-cheese"],["Hot dog","ingredient/hot-dog"],["Hot dog bun","ingredient/hot-dog-bun"],["Sautéed onions","ingredient/sauteed-onions"]]},{"h":"More from Western American cuisine","links":[["Crab Louie","dish/crab-louie"],["Dutch baby pancake","dish/dutch-baby-pancake"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/38/Seattle_Dog.jpg/500px-Seattle_Dog.jpg","w":500,"h":642,"by":"Toohool","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seattle_Dog.jpg"}},"ingredient/trout":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/trout","n":"Trout","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Trout is a generic common name for numerous species of carnivorous freshwater fishes belonging to the genera Oncorhynchus, Salmo, and Salvelinus, all of which are members of the subfamily Salmoninae in the family Salmonidae. The word trout is also used for some similar-shaped but non-salmonid fish, such as the spotted seatrout/speckled trout (Cynoscion nebulosus, which is actually a croaker)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-trout"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trout"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["North Korean cuisine","cuisine/north-korean-cuisine",[["Sungeo-guk","dish/sungeo-guk"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Flathead grey mullet","ingredient/flathead-grey-mullet"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/2e/Salmo_trutta.jpg/500px-Salmo_trutta.jpg","w":500,"h":625,"by":"Eric Engbretson for U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Salmo_trutta.jpg"}},"dish/timphan":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/timphan","n":"Timphan","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Timphan  or jeumphan is a steamed banana dumpling, a traditional kue specialty of Aceh, Indonesia usually served during Eid or other special occasions. Ingredients to make timphan consists of glutinous rice flour, ground banana and coconut milk. All of this materials are then mixed and stirred until a thick as a dough. The banana-rice flour dough is spread lengthwise and then it filled with sweetened serikaya or grated coconut mixed with sugar. Then the dough is wrapped in banana leaves and steamed for an hour."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-timphan"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timphan"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Acehnese cuisine","cuisine/acehnese-cuisine"],["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":9,"links":[["Banana","ingredient/banana"],["Banana leaf","ingredient/banana-leaf"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Latundan banana","ingredient/latundan-banana"],["Pandan","ingredient/pandan"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Acehnese cuisine","links":[["Keumamah","dish/keumamah"],["Meuseukat","dish/meuseukat"],["Mie aceh","dish/mie-aceh"],["Mie caluk","dish/mie-caluk"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/16/Timphan.jpg/500px-Timphan.jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"Azhar Ilyas","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Timphan.jpg"}}}